  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains parts of three programs (tail of a Cyber Operations sequence, BS in Cybersecurity Management and Policy, and the start of BS in Cybersecurity Technology). Only the Cybersecurity Management and Policy program has a complete requirement table, so this ledger covers that program; confirm this is the intended program.",
    "Residency rules are stated only at the degree level and are not tied to specific courses: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) must be completed at UMGC; half the credits in the major must be completed at UMGC; at least 15 upper-level credits (courses numbered 300–499) must be completed at UMGC. No individual requirement is marked institution-only.",
    "At least half the credits for the major must be earned through graded coursework. A minimum grade of C is required in major courses, and a 2.0 overall GPA is required. These constraints are not represented as ledger lines.",
    "Course prerequisites and course descriptions for the major courses are not included in the capture.",
    "The capture does not specify which upper-level courses qualify beyond the listed discipline prefixes for the 9-credit major elective block (sequencing examples: CIFS 305, CSIA 310, CMIT 425).",
    "The general education Mathematics block allows 'a mathematics course approved by the department'. The approved list is not included in the capture.",
    "The capture does not state whether recommended courses in the sequencing table (e.g., CAPL 398A, PACE 111T, LIBS 150, CMIT 202) are required. They are treated as recommendations within the general education and elective blocks."
  ],
